# This repo makes byte-level reproducibility claims about generated artefacts:
#   "npm run seed twice -> identical SHA-256"
#   "a bare `node prism.mjs demo` rebuilds docs/DEMO-TRANSCRIPT.md byte-for-byte"
#   "npm run review:seed reproduces docs/reports/review.md from a fresh clone"
#
# Those claims are only checkable if git hands every clone the same bytes it
# committed. With core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) a fresh clone checks
# out CRLF, the generators write LF, and the hashes differ for a reason that has
# nothing to do with the engine - which is exactly the kind of unverifiable claim
# this project exists to avoid. So: store LF, check out LF, everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch these even if a future contributor's tooling disagrees.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
